      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Alex Mitchell limps off with suspected hamstring pull, major doubt for Australia",
          "body": "England's scrum-half problems deepened at Franklin's Gardens, where Alex Mitchell limped off in Northampton's 28-14 win over Gloucester with what looked like another hamstring problem. It is his fourth hamstring injury of the year, after setbacks at an England camp in May and in the summer Test against Fiji. Archie McParland, his Northampton team-mate, was left out of the matchday squad with a calf injury picked up at England's camp. That leaves Borthwick's options thinner at No 9 before the autumn opener against Australia."
        },
