      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury update",
          "heading": "Ireland say Sam Prendergast is 'optimistic' to face Argentina after wrist injury",
          "body": "Sam Prendergast has stepped up his training in recent days, with assistant coach Paul O'Connell confirming the out-half has been jumping in and out of non-contact and close-to-full-contact sessions. \"I'm not 100% sure, but he looks like he could be OK,\" O'Connell said. The wrist injury came last month, and Prendergast appears to be the only injury concern, with Jimmy O'Brien back in full training after a concussion. Management's update says they are \"optimistic\" he will be available for selection."
        },
