          "kicker": "Injury watch",
          "heading": "Pumas' opponents 'optimistic' Sam Prendergast will be fit for opener",
          "body": "Sam Prendergast appears to be winning his fitness race, with Ireland assistant coach Paul O'Connell saying management are 'optimistic' the out-half will be available. The 23-year-old, who picked up a wrist injury before Leinster's interpro with Munster last month, has stepped up his training, and O'Connell said: 'So, I'm not 100% sure, but he looks like he could be OK.' Prendergast appears to be Ireland's only injury concern, with Jimmy O'Brien back in full training after a concussion, so Argentina may face a near-full-strength side at the Aviva Stadium."
