          "kicker": "Wallabies hopefuls",
          "heading": "Bledisloe debutant McLaughlin-Phillips leads Australia A to 52-0 win over USA",
          "body": "Australia A completed a clean sweep of the USA in New Jersey, after a thumping opener in Nashville. McLaughlin-Phillips led the way, scoring a try, setting up at least three others and finishing with 17 points. Mac Grealy, name-dropped by Les Kiss over the weekend, was one of several backs with five-pointers, while Nick Frost, Will Harris and Toby Macpherson stole four lineouts in the first half. The hosts were 33-0 down at the break."
        },
